---
import Button from '../ui/Button.astro';
import { site } from '../../data/site';

const symptoms = [
  'Neck stiffness or reduced range of motion',
  'Headaches that started after the accident',
  'Numbness or tingling in the arms or hands',
  'Shoulder or upper back pain',
  'Lower back pain or tightness',
  'Dizziness or trouble concentrating',
  "Pain that's getting worse instead of better",
  'Trouble sleeping or turning your head to drive',
];
---

<section class="section feeling" aria-labelledby="feeling-title">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="feeling__inner">
      <div class="feeling__head">
        <p class="eyebrow">If you feel fine, read this</p>
        <h2 id="feeling-title" class="h2">Feeling okay after a crash doesn't mean you're okay.</h2>
        <p class="lead">
          Adrenaline is good at hiding things. Plenty of people walk away from an accident feeling fine, then wake up
          two days later with a stiff neck, a headache that won't quit, or pain running down an arm. That's normal, and
          it's why getting checked early matters even when nothing hurts yet.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="feeling__body">
        <ul class="feeling__list">
          {symptoms.map((s) => <li>{s}</li>)}
        </ul>
        <p class="title-16">Any of these showing up days or weeks later is worth an exam. So is none of them.</p>
        <p class="card-sand feeling__note">
          There's a practical reason to come in early too. The longer the gap between the accident and your first
          visit, the harder it gets to connect the injury to the crash. Getting documented early protects both your
          recovery and your claim.
        </p>
      </div>

      <Button href={site.ctaHref}>Check my coverage</Button>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .feeling__inner {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 40px;
    max-width: 778px;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }
  .feeling__head { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 16px; width: 100%; }
  .feeling__head .lead { color: var(--text-muted); }
  .feeling__body { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 32px; width: 100%; }
  .feeling__list { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 16px; }
  .feeling__list li {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 10px;
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--text-heading);
  }
  .feeling__list li::before {
    content: '';
    flex: none;
    width: 8px;
    height: 8px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--green-700);
    box-shadow: 0 8px 16px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.12), inset 0 8px 10px #637953;
  }
  .feeling__note {
    padding: 24px;
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--text-strong);
  }
  @media (max-width: 767px) {
    .feeling__head { text-align: center; }
  }
</style>
